{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00056 - MONDO_17893",
  "verbalization": "Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a chain of indications involving Mitoxantrone. The drug is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia with Npm1 or Cebpa somatic mutations, and both of these subtypes are linked to Mitoxantrone. Mitoxantrone, in turn, is indicated for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, suggesting a potential pathway where Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin may influence the treatment of this condition through its interaction with Mitoxantrone. The shared use of Mitoxantrone in both contexts implies a possible mechanistic link, though the exact role of Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin remains unclear. The evidence supports a relationship through the indirect pathway of Mitoxantrone, but the direct mechanism by which Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin contributes to this relationship remains an area of further investigation.",
